      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables\n    maturities = [1, 2, 3, 4]\n    yields = [2.0, 2.5, 3.0, 3.5]\n    midpoint_q3 = 2.5\n\n    # Calculate the linearly interpolated yield between Q2 and Q3\n    estimated_yield = yields[1] + (\n        (midpoint_q3 - maturities[1])\n        * (yields[2] - yields[1])\n        / (maturities[2] - maturities[1])\n    )\n\n    # Return the answer rounded to two decimal places\n    return round(estimated_yield, 2)\n```",
